  collect 2840 x62 anywhere gather Mining 1

step Engineering recipes at 100
  tip Back to an Engineering trainer: Practice Lock (from 100) and Silver Contact (from 90). A Mining trainer also teaches Smelt Bronze (2s) and Smelt Tin (50c): smelting at a forge raises Mining too, so smelt what you mine.
  learn 8334
  learn 3973
  learn 2659
  learn 3304

step Practice Lock to 125
  tip Practice Lock is orange at 100 (yellow 115, green 122, grey 130): about 31 crafts to 125, up to 36 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 1 Bronze Bar, 2 Handful of Copper Bolts and 1 Weak Flux. Make the 12 Handful of Copper Bolts first. Use the 50 Handful of Copper Bolts you made earlier; the counts above leave them out. Practice Locks sell to rogues, or open them yourself. Needs an anvil nearby. If you got here without learning Handful of Copper Bolts, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3922
  craft 3922 x12
  craft 8334 until 125

step Mining 117-125: Tin
  tip Mining 117 to 125 before Heavy Blasting Powder: its Heavy Stone come from Mining 125. The area also gives about 15 Copper Ore, 10 Tin Ore, 10 Rough Stone and 5 Coarse Stone: keep them, the next stretches use them. The window lists the areas for your level, best first: the arrow leads to the one you pick and rests once you are in it; each keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns.
